<CourseLayout
  title="Twelve weeks"
  kicker="Teaching programme"
  description="One argument in four blocks. Each week takes the same small C program a step
    further from its source and asks what is left of its meaning."
>
  <p>
    The course runs a two-hour studio every week, and a spine lecture at the start of each
    block. Weeks are cumulative: week 10 is only legible because week 9 built the dispatcher,
    and week 9 is only legible because week 6 separated a genuine branch from an injected one.
    If you are dipping in, read the block claim first.
  </p>

  <p><strong>The question the twelve weeks answer together:</strong> {courseQuestion}</p>

  <h2>Four words we keep apart</h2>
  <p>
    Almost every wrong conclusion in this field is one of these four being mistaken for
    another. They are the vocabulary of every week, every ledger and every marking rubric
    here.
  </p>
